                 }
            }
        }
    });
    ParseInstallation.getCurrentInstallation().saveInBackground();
</code></pre>

<p>Hope this Helps in some way.</p>

Q: How do I pass --homedir to git when signing using GPG? A: <p>To selectively have only <code>git</code> use GPG with a different home directory, but still use the default home directory for other applications, you can use a wrapper script:</p>
<pre class="lang-bash prettyprint-override"><code>#!/bin/sh
export GNUPGHOME=&quot;${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-~/.config}/gnupg-trezor&quot;
exec gpg &quot;$@&quot;
</code></pre>
<p>Mark it as executable, then configure <code>git</code> to use this script instead of the default GPG command:</p>
<pre class="lang-shellsession prettyprint-override"><code>$ git config --global gpg.program &quot;&lt;path-to-wrapper-script&gt;&quot;
</code></pre>
<p>This is useful to sign commits using a hardware wallet, while still using software keys for e-mail, for instance.</p>
